                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 2,
                "retweet_count": 2,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "I had the pleasure of sitting down with the Roswell Children's Cancer and Blood Disorders Center to discuss the current landscape of healthcare and the importance of supporting medical research to improve the health and quality of life of people living in Western New York.\u00a0\n\nHealth disparities have persisted within communities of color in Buffalo, and cuts to Medicaid, Medicare, and NIH funding will only increase these disparities and hinder people\u2019s ability to treat genetic and chronic diseases.\n\nWe must provide compassion, relief, and hope to patients and populations who are being consistently overlooked and denied comprehensive healthcare. We must defend and preserve federal health assistance programs that are effectively bridging the gap between coverage and care.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
                "timestamp": 1752700738,
                "view_count": 479
            },
            {
                "attached_links_expanded_url": null,
                "attached_links_url": null,
                "attached_medias_preview_url": [
                    "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/GxiWsi1XAAA4jhW.jpg?name=small",
